# Localization — translate with the feature

User-visible strings live in **`src/<Plugin>/Localization/*.xaml`**. English (`en_US.xaml`) is the source of truth and the runtime fallback, but **every Playnite Crowdin locale file must still get the same keys, translated**.

## When this applies

Any new or changed setting, hover field, preview sample, button, tab, tooltip, or error string. Do not ship a feature that only updates `en_US.xaml`.

## Required steps

1. Add or edit the key in **`en_US.xaml`** first (`LOC<Plugin>_…`).
2. Copy that **same key** into **every** other `Localization/*.xaml` in that extension (same key order as English).
3. **Translate** each locale. Do not leave English except:
   - Brand / product names (Playnite, Steam, Phosphor, Unicons, Huge Icons)
   - Format placeholders (`{0}`) and XML newlines (`&#10;`)
   - Values that are identical in that language (unit letters `s`/`m`/`h` when that is the local abbreviation; numeric samples)
4. Escape `&` as `&amp;`. Keep `↑↓` and `{0}` unchanged.

```xml
<!-- ❌ BAD: new setting only in English -->
<sys:String x:Key="LOCGameHoverDetails_Settings_FieldColumns">Field columns</sys:String>
<!-- other locales still missing the key, or still say "Field columns" -->

<!-- ✅ GOOD: same key in every locale, translated -->
<!-- en_US --><sys:String x:Key="LOCGameHoverDetails_Settings_FieldColumns">Field columns</sys:String>
<!-- de_DE --><sys:String x:Key="LOCGameHoverDetails_Settings_FieldColumns">Feldspalten</sys:String>
```

Reuse words already in that locale file (hover/icon/background equivalents). Autogrid has no loc files today; if it gains UI strings, add the full Playnite locale set the same way.
